# /etc/default/earlyoom -- fleet-wide, all four GB10 nodes.
#
# Install on each node, then: sudo systemctl enable --now earlyoom
#
# Why every value here is what it is (2026-09-04, after three nodes wedged):
#
# GB10 is unified memory. NVRM allocates the model against MemFree and those
# pages are PINNED -- neither droppable nor swappable. So on a loaded node
# the kernel sees ~55 GiB of unreclaimable anon, ~150 MB of file cache, and
# a 16 GiB swap that never fills. Two consequences shape this file:
#
# 1. A PERCENTAGE swap threshold can never be met. earlyoom kills only when
#    memory AND swap are both below their thresholds; with SwapFree pinned
#    at ~100% the AND is false forever. The previous "-m 2 -s 2" was
#    unfireable by construction. -s 100 makes swap non-binding so memory
#    alone decides.
#
# 2. The kernel min watermark on these boxes is 4.0 GiB (srv3's OOM dump:
#    "free:4.00 GiB min:4.00 GiB all_unreclaimable? yes"). Below it, fork()
#    blocks in direct reclaim with nothing to reclaim, sshd stops opening
#    sessions, and the node is lost to everything but a power cycle. The
#    floor here is ABSOLUTE and sits above that line: 6 GiB. It is also
#    below what a healthy boot leaves -- the launcher's memfree preflight
#    reserves 10 GiB -- so a good boot never crosses it. "-m 2" (2.4 GiB)
#    was under the watermark: by the time it could fire, it could not fork.
#
# Both stages are set explicitly. earlyoom derives the SIGKILL thresholds as
# HALF of the SIGTERM ones when they are not given, which on the first
# install produced "SIGKILL when mem <= 2.47% and swap <= 50.00%" -- a swap
# condition this fleet never meets (see above) and a memory line under the
# watermark. So: SIGTERM at 6 GiB, SIGKILL at 4.5 GiB (still above the
# 4.0 GiB line), swap non-binding for both.
#
# Kill target: the engine, on purpose. When the floor IS crossed the engine
# is the runaway, and the alternative is losing the node, which loses the
# engine anyway. The ledger's earlier "--avoid vllm" was the right call
# against PERCENTAGE thresholds that fired on healthy resident models; an
# absolute floor below healthy steady state removes that failure mode, so
# the preference flips. The management plane stays protected.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-M 6291456,4718592 -s 100,100 -r 60 -n --prefer '(VLLM::Worker|vllm|pt_main_thread|python3)' --avoid '(sshd|systemd|dockerd|containerd|tailscaled|deneb-gateway|sparkfleet|earlyoom)'"
